Subject: [P6] Dispatch M in {3,4} to an MB=4 DPAS tile (B6 fix candidate)
Base-commit: 15ded2f3add148c4db3c900cba7de878238f53bc
Status: local-only draft; PROVISIONAL — NOT FOR PUBLIC HEADLINE
Applies after 0001..0006. Anchors: csrc/exl3_ops.sycl dispatch_dpas :133-143,
dpas_nt/globals :167-176, exl3_gemm_small MB selection :291-307 (post-series),
setter block :797-803, bindings :826-833.
Author: substitute for b70-kernel-engineer (provider quota), 2026-09-29.
Static authoring only; NOT BUILT / NOT GPU-TESTED.

Defect (RL-098, results/2026/09/b70-b6-microprobe-20260929/RESULTS.md): the
M=4 DPAS path loses a uniform 8-15 points of pin-fraction vs the M=1 vector
GEMV on identical bytes across every family (verify pass 34.46 ms vs 29.44 ms).
Hypothesis encoded: M in {3,4} pads to the MB=8 tile, wasting ~half the DPAS
tile work. This patch dispatches M in {3,4} to DpasKernel<K,CB,4,NT=4> by
default; exl3_set_dpas_mb4(0) restores the padded MB=8 path for same-build A/B.

Legality (D1-style derivation): the tile decode geometry is MB-independent —
Geo<K>: K4 -> g=4,D=1,V=8,G=32,W=32; K6 -> g=2,D=3,V=16,G=16,W=48; K3 -> g=1,
D=3,V=32,G=8,W=24; P=V==8?4:(V==16?2:1) and A_=G/P=8 unchanged (asserted at
exl3_esimd.h:605). MB enters only row-block extents: RC = MB<8?MB:8 = 4 makes
the rb-loop run once with a legal dpas<8,4>; Am = MB*16 = 64 fp16; acc =
MB*16*NT = 256 fp32 lanes (vs 512 at MB8 — strictly less GRF pressure). Host
side: dpas_nt(4)=EXL3_DPAS4_NT=4 = dpas_nt(8), so n_strips, m_blocks, P and rps
are identical to the MB8 path and strip coverage needs tiles_n % NT == 0 —
tiles_n in {64,320,384,640,768,1088,15520} all divide by 4 (static_assert
restricts NT to {2,4,8}; min routed tiles_n is 64). launch_dpas's
xh-rows==m_blocks*MB TORCH_CHECK holds: host pads Mp=4. FUSED path untouched
(fused_small still instantiates MB=8; static_assert(MB==8) intact). Every
compiled (K,cb) pair gets the case-4 instantiation: K4/K6 unconditionally,
K3 + remaining codebooks only where EXL3_ALL_CODEBOOKS compiles them.

Numerics: per output element the fp32 accumulate chain is unchanged — RC
selects rows-per-instruction, not the K accumulation order; same r-ordered
dpas sequence, same P/rps split-K, same n_strips, pad rows never stored.
MB4 output is expected BIT-IDENTICAL to MB8 for identical xh rows; the spec
asserts exact equality, with the RL-099 amended tolerance
(mx <= max(0.01+0.05*rms_row, 1 ulp of the output dtype)) as the declared
fallback only. Zero-tolerance trellis/one-hot gates are on the vector/raw
paths and untouched. exl3_gemm_raw deliberately keeps the padded MB=8
geometry — a fixed MB8 reference for the identity check.

Capture-safety: no new host sync, no new allocation site, no new scratch
kind; xh shrinks (Mp 8->4 for M in {3,4}); part {P,M,N} unchanged. Inherited
allocation sites unchanged — whole-op D3 HOLD stands. The runtime flag is a
host-side launch decision and must be set before graph capture.
Known upstream wart (unchanged): under -DEXL3_DPAS_MB4, exl3_gemm_raw's MBp
padding lacks an MB4 arm, so its MB4 dispatch would fail the xh TORCH_CHECK;
stock builds never define it and the raw path is unaffected.

Isolated-op A/B spec (for the bench window, NOT run): tests/mb4_ab_spec.txt —
down_proj 17408->5120 and qkv 5120->12288 at M in {3,4}, MB8 vs MB4 via the
runtime lever on one build, XPU-graph + bulk XPU-event methodology per
RL-098; PRIMARY GATE: recover >=5 points of pin-fraction on both families at
both M; identity check exact-or-amended-tolerance as stated above.

diff --git a/csrc/exl3_ops.sycl b/csrc/exl3_ops.sycl
--- a/csrc/exl3_ops.sycl
+++ b/csrc/exl3_ops.sycl
@@ -138,9 +138,10 @@
