@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@
+P6 — MB=4 DPAS isolated-op A/B specification (FUTURE EXECUTION ONLY)
+PROVISIONAL — NOT FOR PUBLIC HEADLINE
+Base: 0xSero/exl3xpu 15ded2f3add148c4db3c900cba7de878238f53bc + series 0001..0007.
+Classification: local-only spec; NO measurement was performed or claimed here.
+Capture status: the patched dispatch adds no captured-region allocation site and
+no host sync; the xh scratch SHRINKS (Mp 8 -> 4 rows for M in {3,4}); part
+{P,M,N} is unchanged because dpas_nt(4)=EXL3_DPAS4_NT=4 = dpas_nt(8) keeps
+n_strips, m_blocks and P identical. Whole-op capture safety remains D3 HOLD
+(inherited allocation sites unchanged in kind). g_dpas_mb4 is a launch-time
+host decision and MUST be set before graph capture.
+
+1. Defect under test (RL-098, results/2026/09/b70-b6-microprobe-20260929/RESULTS.md)
+   The M=4 DPAS path loses a uniform 8-15 points of pin-fraction vs the M=1
+   vector GEMV on identical bytes across every family; the verify pass is
+   34.46 ms vs 29.44 ms M=1 for the same 13.12 GB. Hypothesis: M in {3,4}
+   pads to the MB=8 tile and wastes ~half the DPAS tile work. P6 dispatches
+   M in {3,4} to DpasKernel<K,CB,4,EXL3_DPAS4_NT=4> (RC=4, one dpas<8,4>
+   per tile instead of one dpas<8,8>; acc 256 vs 512 fp32 lanes).
+
+2. Cells
+   - down_proj family: Kdim=17408 -> N=5120, K=4 cb=2 (trellis (1088,320,64),
+     44.6 MB/call) — largest single-family byte weight.
+   - qkv family: Kdim=5120 -> N=12288, K=4 cb=2 (trellis (320,768,64),
+     31.5 MB/call).
+   - M in {3, 4} on each family (MTP3 verify is M=4 rows; M=3 exercises the
+     partial-row store path with a zero-padded xh row).
+   - Optional confirmation cell: K=6 lm_head 5120 -> 248320 at M=4 (the only
+     K=6 family; verifies the MB4 instantiation on the K6 build/decode path).
+
+3. Arms (single patched build, runtime lever — no rebuild needed)
+   - A = incumbent tile: exl3_set_dpas_mb4(0) -> the padded MB=8 path.
+   - B = candidate tile: exl3_set_dpas_mb4(1) -> the MB=4 path (default).
+   - Secondary fixed MB8 reference: exl3_gemm_raw(path=1) keeps the padded
+     MB=8 geometry by design on this patch, for an independent MB8 output.
+   - Optional third arm: a series-0001..0006 library as the stock control.
+
+4. Method (RL-098 harness methodology, unchanged)
+   - harness_graphprobe.py protocol: 16-32 calls captured in one
+     torch.xpu.XPUGraph, >=12 replay timings, median per call; plus the bulk
+     >=200-iteration XPU-event cross-check. Same read-only artifact, GPU0 /
+     ZE_AFFINITY_MASK=0, power caps as-found and restored, no engine/server.
+   - Metric: trellis bytes / XPU-event median time = GB/s, reported both as
+     % of the 608 GB/s pin floor and % of the 521 GB/s measured-achievable
+     read reference, per the RL-098 convention.
+   - Set the flag, capture the graph, measure; flip flag, re-capture, measure.
+     Never compare across a live capture boundary.
+
+5. Gates (pre-declared, frozen before execution)
+   - PRIMARY SPEED GATE: arm B recovers >= 5 points of pin-fraction vs arm A
+     on BOTH families at BOTH M=3 and M=4 (e.g. down_proj M=4: 57.5% -> >=62.5%
+     of pin). A miss on any of the four cells fails the gate.
+   - NUMERICAL IDENTITY: fixed identical inputs, arm B output vs arm A output.
+     Expected bit-identical: RC changes only rows-per-dpas-instruction (8 -> 4),
+     not the per-element fp32 accumulation order — same r-ordered accumulate
+     chain, same P/rps/n_strips, pad rows are never stored. Declared fallback
+     if a boundary-flip excursion appears: the amended dense gate
+     mx <= max(0.01 + 0.05*rms_row, 1 ulp of the OUTPUT dtype at the reference
+     element) per RL-099. Excursions beyond that bound = FAIL; no post-hoc
+     relaxation.
+   - EXACT-PATH GATES UNTOUCHED: trellis reconstruction and one-hot decode
+     remain zero-tolerance (P3 battery); this patch does not touch them.
+   - KILL: XPUGraph capture failure, TORCH_CHECK/dispatch failure, or output
+     corruption on any cell.
+   - If the primary gate passes: P6 becomes the champion-dispatch input for a
+     matched end-to-end verify-pass A/B (RL-098 §6 pricing: closing half the
+     M=4 gap is ~2.5 ms/verify pass). No adoption claim from the isolated op.
